# Cloud session vs local Terminal (permanent)

**Detect session type first.** If this agent is a **Cloud Agent / background cloud session** (remote VM, no Mac filesystem):

1. **Remind the admin clearly:** “This session is running in the **cloud**, not on your Mac.”
2. **Do not ask the admin to paste/run Terminal commands on their machine** as if this session were local.
3. For anything that **must** run on the Mac (ASC keys under `/Users/…`, local sandbox, Neo Private Keys, desktop-only tools):
   - Tell them to **open or continue a local Cursor session** on the machine that has the files/sandbox.
   - Ask that **local session** to issue the command in **its local sandbox** (with the right permissions).
4. Prefer doing cloud-capable work **in this cloud session** (git, gh, wrangler with cloud tokens, production curls) instead of bouncing shell snippets to the admin.

If the session **is** local (desktop/laptop with the repo), run Terminal commands yourself in the local sandbox — do not offload them to the admin unless approval or a secret only they can supply is required.
